1|0@askgaybros^1438524491#ctouuc8:GeorgeGnyc02$:I don't think this has to be a hopeless scenario. Hopefully a close relative or family friend can talk some sense into them when they ask where you are. I find most very homophobic people are more afraid of what other say then what they actually believe. They feel they are looked on as having a gay son in the neighborhood or community. Having a "gay son" looks bad in their eyes, but being a neglectful parent makes them look 1000 times worse. Hopefully someone can talk some sense into them and you can be atleast on speaking terms By the use of the term university Im guessing you are not American. Isn't schooling free or very cheap. Try and enroll somewhere where you can stay at the dorms and get a part time job through the school or an internship. Looks for possibilities. 
1|0@askgaybros^1438525213#ctov4c8:chizhiks$:Not, I'm not American. In my country education is expensive. You have to study good and I mean very very very good, spend day and night by the books for the government to finance your studies. Otherwise you have to pay for it yourself. And it's often more than thousand euros for one academic year. I don't have such money, neither do I have the time to become a top student, finding some kind of a job is more important right now.
