13|0@askgaybros^1438512438#ctorioa:zemien$:Stay strong! You have your bf and his family, and your online support network is right here. What you can do right now is to start contributing to your bf's home. Help with chores, tidy up the garden, make breakfast, even small things like bringing in the mail will help you feel productive and not like you're overstaying as a guest. More ideas: if you can drive, offer to do groceries. Pay attention to what they need help with (I stay on my own, there's always something I could use a hand with) e.g. laundry, minor repairs around the house, tech support. Whatever your skills can offer!
10|0@askgaybros^1438506845#ctoqdrg:norgay87$:This sounds like a hopeless scenario. Right now. Your boyfriend is right. Everything will be okay. If I was in your shoes, I would try to look for any kind of organization that could help with your further education, that's really important. Maybe use this as an excuse to study abroad, in my country, Norway, universities and colleges are free, even for foreigners. Only a small fee at about 100 USD per semester. Try to look for solutions instead of problems. The world is full of people who are willing and able to help you, you just have to find them. Best of luck and my warmest wishes for you! ❤️
